Project: Kixora. Node 22, npm only (never bun).
Never print, request, or commit secrets. Never push to main.
Work on a branch; PR into develop; test-and-build must be green.
Windows PowerShell: never use && ; run one command per line.
Before finishing run, one per line: npx tsc --noEmit, then npx eslint . --max-warnings 0, then npm run test, then npm run build.
Source of truth is the code, not docs claiming "complete".
Do not touch unrelated files. Show a diff summary before committing.
Do not run npm ci or npm install unless I ask.
Stack & versions
• Coding conventions / style
• Required verification commands (tests, lint, typecheck)
• Files/directories it must never touch
• “Always run tests after changes and report results”
• “Prefer smallest viable diff”
- Always work on the smallest possible change.
- Never invent files, functions, or libraries that do not exist.
- After every important change, run the tests and show me the result.
- If you are not sure about something, stop and ask me.
- Do not refactor code that is not related to the current task.
- Prefer clear, simple code that matches the existing style of the project.
- Always start in Plan mode for new tasks.
- Keep changes small and reversible.